<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83408" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλαγκ-τός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ός</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Ag.</u>
			593
		</span></i> : (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλάζω</span> A) :—poet.
			Adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wandering, roaming</i>, of
			ships, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				277
			</span></i> (lyr.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλαγκτὰ δ᾽ ὡσεί τις νεφέλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					961
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ὕδωρ</span>, of the
			Euripús, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.73
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphil.
			</span></i>) ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰός</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				6.75
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλαγκτὰν
			ὁδόν</span> a <i>devious</i> route, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hymn.Is.</u>
				149
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἄστρὰ,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλάνητες</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Eph.
			</span></i> ap. Theo Sm.<i><span class="en">
				p.140
			</span></i> H. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>wandering in mind, erring, distraught</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				21.363
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				593
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πλαγκταὶ πέτραι</span> rocks near Scylla
			and Charybdis, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.59s
			</span></i>qq., <i><span class="en">
				23.327
			</span></i>; later identified with the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Συμπληγάδες</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κυάνεαι</span> of the Bosporus, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.85
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Peripl.M.Eux.</u>
				25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eratosth.
			</span></i> ap. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				2
			</span></i>, etc.; but also with the volcanic islands of Lipari, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.924
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				1.9.25
			</span></i>.</div>
